/-!
# Anti-foundation axioms as views

Foundation, Aczel's anti-foundation, Scott's axiom, Finsler's axiom and
Boffa's axiom are five answers to when two pointed graphs picture the same
set. The common core is a regular identification: an equivalence that is a
bisimulation, so the quotient still has a well-defined set of members. Each
axiom is the view that keeps the distinctions that identification keeps.

Forti and Honsell's hyperuniverses, and positive set theory with a universal
set, are outside this development. They are not identifications of pointed
graphs in this family.
-/
